# remote_viewer — project core

You are working on **remote_viewer**, a clean-room low-latency remote desktop (concept like AnyDesk/RustDesk). Crate prefix `vd-*` is internal.

## Goals (priority)

1. Ultra-low latency (LAN p50 ≤ 40 ms glass-to-glass — initial target)
2. Usable on weak nets (1 Mbps / 150 ms RTT / 3–5% loss)
3. Lightweight CPU/RAM
4. Secure by default (E2E, consent)
5. Reliable NAT + relay
6. Windows first

## Ethics (hard)

- Host always shows a visible indicator while viewed/controlled; host can end anytime
- Unattended access = explicit opt-in only
- No hidden mode, process masking, persistence tricks, credential harvesting

## Where things live

- Architecture/protocol: `docs/01_*.md`–`docs/04_*.md`
- Tasks/status: `docs/07_TASKS.md`, `docs/STATUS.md`, `docs/HANDOFF.md`
- ADRs: `docs/adr/`
- Roles/locks: `docs/agents/`
- Hot path crates: `vd-capture`, `vd-codec`, `vd-net`, `vd-rate`, apps agent/viewer

Do not implement stealth RAT features. Prefer stubs returning `Error::NotImplemented` over `todo!()` in test paths.
